     "title": "Overview",
     "bullets": [
      {
       "id": "1a.1",
       "text": "A heatwave struck the town of Verlow from 22 June 2026, with the Provincial Public Health Institute issuing its first warning on 23 June.",
       "confidence": "confirmed",
       "tweet_ids": []
      },
      {
       "id": "1a.2",
       "text": "The heat strained the power grid: Grennet Power issued a warning and deployed crews, the Marnest substation was destroyed and dangerous conditions developed at Hetton Rise and Camber Green.",
       "confidence": "confirmed",
       "tweet_ids": []
      },
      {
       "id": "1a.3",
       "text": "Injuries were confirmed in the town and deaths were attributed to the heatwave and to the warning period, with service at Verlow General Hospital disrupted.",
       "confidence": "confirmed",
       "tweet_ids": []
      },
      {
       "id": "1a.4",
       "text": "The institute deployed and asked for assistance, a meeting was held in Verlow, and Grennet Power revised its policy as the window closed.",
       "confidence": "confirmed",
       "tweet_ids": []
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
